Raise PJSIP and pjmedia limits to fit real browser (WebRTC) SDP.

Chromium/Firefox offers routed through the external media endpoint API
carry more formats and attributes per media line than pjmedia's
defaults (an audio+video Chromium offer has ~80 attributes on the
video m= line, over the default PJMEDIA_MAX_SDP_ATTR of 68). The
parser silently drops the excess, losing rtpmap lines and failing
validation. These offers can also exceed PJSIP's default 4 KiB
transmit buffer, causing the INVITE to fail locally with status 503.

--- a/pjlib/include/pj/config_site.h
+++ b/pjlib/include/pj/config_site.h
@@ -8,5 +8,5 @@
 /*
 * PJSIP settings.
 */
-#define PJSIP_MAX_PKT_LEN                       8000
+#define PJSIP_MAX_PKT_LEN                       16384
 #define PJSIP_TRANSPORT_SERVER_IDLE_TIME        3
@@ -24,3 +24,15 @@
 /* Set permanent permissions on the TURN
    server for all peer candidates */
 #define PJ_ICE_ST_USE_TURN_PERMANENT_PERM       PJ_TRUE
+
+/*
+* PJMEDIA settings.
+* Browser (WebRTC) SDP offers used by the external media endpoint API carry
+* far more formats and attributes per media line than pjmedia's defaults
+* (an audio+video Chromium offer has ~80 attributes on the video m= line,
+* over the default PJMEDIA_MAX_SDP_ATTR of 68). The parser silently drops
+* the excess, losing rtpmap lines and failing validation, so raise the
+* limits to comfortably fit real browser SDP.
+*/
+#define PJMEDIA_MAX_SDP_FMT                     64
+#define PJMEDIA_MAX_SDP_ATTR                    256
